  "issue": {
    "title": "Run CCR automatically on any targeted base branch",
    "body": "## Description\n\nI noticed in https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14717 and other PRs that Copilot Code Review was not triggering automatically. Seems this is because our ruleset only applies when the base branch is `trunk`, which doesn't play right with stacked PRs.\n\n### Expected Outcome\n\nCCR runs automatically regardless of base branch.",
    "comments": [
      {
        "author": "williammartin",
        "body": "Done.\n\n```\ngh api repos/cli/cli/rulesets/4898070 --jq '{name,enforcement,conditions,rules,updated_at}'\n{\"conditions\":{\"ref_name\":{\"exclude\":[],\"include\":[\"~ALL\"]}},\"enforcement\":\"active\",\"name\":\"Copilot Code Review\",\"rules\":[{\"parameters\":{\"review_draft_pull_requests\":true,\"review_on_push\":false},\"type\":\"copilot_code_review\"}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-10-19T13:23:13.419+02:00\"}\n```",
